 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "Merged from 2_26-27_r97, 2_28-29_r97 (reviewed) because the boundary between them has no clean audio cut. [2_26-27_r97] Parables (26) and the covenant-breakers (27). The disbelievers' question (26:24) gets no gloss; the answer (26:29) is explained. The seal (covenant) undraws at «يقطعون». [2_28-29_r97] Life, death and creation (28-29). No motif or gloss on «استوى» (Allah's istiwa); no motif on Allah's attributes. STAGING v4: 26: believers (who know it is the truth) and an uncountable group of disbelievers who object («فيقولون», shake heads); nothing on the Name. 27: the covenant-breakers turn away and walk away from their kin on «يقطعون» (Muyassar: كقطع الأرحام); wind on «يفسدون». 28 (life, death, resurrection) and 29 (creation of the heavens, istiwa) stay ambient: Allah's acts and the unseen; in 29 the mountain now ends before «ثم استوى» and the stars before «وهو بكل شيء عليم»."
 },
